      "PerformanceComplete": {
        "description": "Thu Oct 8 (X0): the client now uploads headerless 16-bit PCM\nchunks (see ``elums/ingest/wav.py``'s docstring for why), so\n`complete` needs the capture sample rate to build a real WAV\nheader once \u2014 unlike MediaRecorder's self-describing WebM, raw PCM\nchunks carry no format metadata at all. Defaults to 48000 (the\ncommon desktop `AudioContext` default) only for backward\ncompatibility with any in-flight pre-X0 client; real callers\nalways send the `AudioContext.sampleRate` they actually captured\nat (\u00a710.4: never force `sampleRate`, so this varies by device).",
        "properties": {
          "sample_rate": {
            "default": 48000,
            "title": "Sample Rate",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "title": "PerformanceComplete",
        "type": "object"
      },
